          "message": "The JWT matcher misses valid compact JWTs with short or empty segments, allowing them into logs and traces.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Log messages, log properties, and trace attributes pass through ScrubText, but Jwt() matches only when all three dot-separated segments contain at least four characters.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs or traces the valid unsecured JWT `eyJhbGciOiJub25lIn0.e30.`. Its empty signature segment fails the regex, so the token reaches the provider or exporter without redaction. This violates the required JWT-shape redaction (OWASP A09:2025)."
          }
        }
